  "cot_trace": " I'm thinking through a straightforward approach: take the given edges and augment them with additional connections to ensure every vertex reaches at least degree 4 and the graph achieves vertex connectivity of 4. The simplest method would be to layer in a Hamiltonian-like structure with some extra edges to hit those connectivity requirements.\n\nActually, I'll use a circulant graph construction\u2014adding edges (i, i+1 mod 18), (i, i+2 mod 18), (i, i+3 mod 18), and (i, i+4 mod 18)\u2014which creates an 8-regular, 8-connected graph. Taking the union of this with the given edges guarantees we'll exceed the connectivity threshold of 4, so I can verify this works.",
